{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1776807351,"nonce":"j7r36iosMrQ96ie/d+VHNjjuRgo=","title":"Pre-review rebase fails on mounted files - move rebase to host","message":"## Problem\n\nThe pre-review rebase runs inside the container (`core/rebase.py`), but WORKFLOW.md is bind-mounted. When the agent branch includes WORKFLOW.md changes, git cannot unlink the mounted file during rebase:\n\n```\nerror: unable to unlink old 'WORKFLOW.md': Device or resource busy\nerror: could not detach HEAD\n```\n\nThis causes a rebase loop: session restarts to fix conflict → fails again → repeat until max-resumes.\n\n## Example\n\nSession `review-b7e7dee7b0bd` hit max-resumes ($2.82 wasted) because the rebase kept failing on the mounted WORKFLOW.md. The reviewer had already approved the code.\n\n## Root Cause\n\n`core/rebase.py` runs inside the container where:\n- WORKFLOW.md is bind-mounted read-only\n- Git operations that need to replace mounted files fail\n\n## Solution\n\nMove pre-review rebase to run on the **host** side:\n1. After container exits with `done:pending-review`, host does the rebase\n2. If rebase fails, host can handle it (no mounted files)\n3. Only launch review session after successful rebase\n\n## Files to modify\n\n- `core/rebase.py` → extract rebase logic to be callable from host\n- `host/launch.py` or `host/watcher/review_orchestrator.py` → call rebase before launching review\n- `core/post_run.py` → remove rebase call from container side\n\n## Tests\n\n- `test_rebase_runs_on_host_not_container`\n- `test_rebase_failure_does_not_loop_session`\n\nREQ: REQ-026 (session lifecycle)","files":null}]}